WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.380
Привет!

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.560
That means hello in Russian.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:10.280
Welcome to Privet Ruski, episode 16 for April 30, 2026.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:16.160
I'm Olya, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.040
Ready?

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.200
Поехали!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.640
That means let's go.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.980
Сегодня мы говорим о Пагоде.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.260
That means today we are talking about the weather.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.940
Our word of the day is pagoda.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.740
Поехали, да, погода.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.320
It means weather.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.260
It sounds like pogostik.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.540
Imagine jumping up and down because the weather keeps changing.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:43.920
Repeat after me.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.460
Поехали, да, погода.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.620
Now try this sentence.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.420
Какая сегодня пагода.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.560
That means what is the weather like today?

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.100
Great job!

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.440
You just asked about the weather in Russian.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.060
Next let's build more words around this theme.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.780
First comes Сонсе.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.440
Солнце.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.600
It means sun.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:13.420
Think solar.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.480
Both words come from the same ancient root for the bright star in the sky.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.040
Repeat after me.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.140
Солнце.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.520
Солнце.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.920
Now we have Небо.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.740
Ни Эх Бо.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.140
Небо.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.620
It means sky.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:34.620
Imagine Небо.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.520
Both words describe the vast space above us.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.180
Repeat after me.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:41.260
Небо.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:42.840
Ни Эх Бо.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.220
Небо.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.320
Look up.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.940
На Небо Бе Ла ОБЛОКО.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.440
That means there is a white cloud in the sky.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.060
ОБЛОКО means cloud.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.320
О КЧБо ЛАХ КОХ.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:54.460
ОБЛОКО.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.100
It sounds like oblong.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.600
Clouds are often soft oblong shapes floating above.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.760
Repeat after me.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:03.920
ОБЛОКО.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.520
О ЖБИ ЛАХ КОХ.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:06.540
ОБЛОКО.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.440
Sometimes the sky changes.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.160
Идёт дождь.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.020
Идёт дождь.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.040
Идёт дождь.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.960
That means rain is falling.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.800
Дождь means rain.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.600
It sounds a little like dodge.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.820
You have to dodge the rain drops.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.740
Repeat after me.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.260
Идёт дождь.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.000
Идёт дождь.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.760
When it is windy, we say, витер.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.080
Вьех тьер.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:38.540
Витер.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.260
It means wind.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.540
Imagine a veteran wind that has been blowing for years and years.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.340
Repeat after me.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.260
Витер.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.640
Вьех тьер.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:51.780
Витер.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.360
Сегодня сильный витер.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.960
That means today there is strong wind.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.940
Now let's talk about how it feels.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:01.080
Типло.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.280
Теп.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.160
Алло.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.560
Типло.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.440
It means warm or warmth.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.400
Think thermal underwear.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.600
Both words are about heat and warmth.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.440
Repeat after me.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:15.120
Типло.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:16.620
Тип-ло.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.140
Тип-ло.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:19.820
Now let's say, тепло.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.260
That means it is warm outside.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.260
The opposite is холодно.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.840
Кол-уд-нух.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:27.900
холодно.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.880
It means it is cold.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.820
It sounds like cold with an extra K-ak at the beginning.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.980
Just at that Russian-aka sound.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:38.560
Repeat after me.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:39.940
холодно.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.020
Кол-уд-нух.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.140
холодно.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.060
Зимой очень холодно.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.240
That means in winter it is very cold.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.160
We also need светит.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.020
Светит.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:51.540
Тит.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:52.800
Светит.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.020
It means shines or is shining.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:56.340
Think light.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.660
Свет in Russian means light.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.340
So the sun gives us sweat.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.460
Repeat after me.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:04.760
Светит.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:06.460
Светит.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:07.780
Светит.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:09.420
Сон-сосветит.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.440
That means the sun is shining.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.760
Now here is a simple grammar bite that makes weather talk easy.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.920
In Russian we almost never say it is.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.940
We just use the weather word by itself.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.260
холодно.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.460
That means it is cold.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:27.400
Тип-ло.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.080
That means it is warm.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.300
It dot dot.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.100
That means rain is going or it is raining.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.220
In English we must say it is raining.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:42.040
In Russian it disappears and the verb to be often disappears too.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.260
This makes sentences shorter and easier once you get used to it.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:51.420
If you can say холодно correctly you are already speaking real Russian weather talk.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:55.900
Russians love to talk about the weather almost as much as British people do.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:59.720
In many parts of Russia the winters are very long and cold.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:03.900
So when spring finally arrives everyone excitedly says Наконец-то.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:05.140
Тип-ло.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.320
That means finally it is warm.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.700
You will often hear people greeting each other with weather comments instead of just hello.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:18.480
It is a friendly way to start a conversation and shows you care about how the other person

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.260
feels that day.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.740
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.340
Want to know a secret about sunset?

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:30.020
Did you know that the Russian word сонс and the English word сон

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.140
are actually the same word.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:37.360
They both come from the ancient proto Indo-European root that meant сон.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.240
This word started in prehistoric times.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:46.820
It traveled through many languages and arrived in old Russian as a lens before becoming the modern сонс.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:54.120
Along the way the L sound softened and the spelling changed but the glowing meaning stayed exactly the same.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.840
But be careful, there is a fun false friend nearby.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.780
The Russian word for light is sweat.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:06.460
It sounds a bit like English sweet but has nothing to do with candy.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:13.320
Next time you see the English word сонс, remember it is cousins with Russian sons.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.320
They both come from that same ancient glowing root.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:22.020
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.640
Do you remember what pagoda means?

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.160
It means weather, what about сонс?

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.760
It means sun.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.000
Try using this sentence three times today.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.500
Сегодня сонс осветит и тепло.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.900
That means today the sun is shining and it is warm.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:42.640
Now change it and say, сегодня холодно идёт дождь.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.540
That means today it is cold and rain is falling.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:52.260
For fun draw a big smiling sun, a cloud with rain drops and a windy tree.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:58.800
Under each picture write the Russian word, then play weather shardas with your family.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:04.460
Act out the weather word and see if they can guess in Russian.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:15.120
Repeat after me, slowly pagoda, pagoda, сонс осветит, сонс осветит, идёт дождь, идёт дождь, тепло.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.860
Типло, you did it.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:23.700
If you understood even one sentence today, you are already speaking Russian.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:25.300
Молодец.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.600
That means well done.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:34.140
Remember every expert started as a beginner, practicing today's words out loud,

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:38.020
even just once, and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.280
See you next time, Пока.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.040
That's Russian for buy.

